---
permalink: /ocr/index.html
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en"><head>
<meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1">
<title>{{ ocr.config.title }}</title>
<meta name="description" content="Documented cross-benchmark OCR scores, pricing and historical release cohorts.">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/css/benchmark.css">
<script>(function(){try{document.documentElement.dataset.theme=localStorage.getItem('bench-theme')||(matchMedia('(prefers-color-scheme: dark)').matches?'dark':'light')}catch(e){}})();</script>
</head><body><main>
<header class="hero"><div><small class="eyebrow">Voshart / Benchmarks</small><h1>{{ ocr.config.title }}</h1><p>{{ ocr.config.description }}</p></div><button class="quiet" id="themeToggle" type="button" aria-label="Toggle light and dark mode">Theme</button></header>
<section class="history-bar" data-release-start="{{ ocr.config.release_start }}" data-snapshot-date="{{ ocr.config.snapshot_date }}" aria-label="Historical model release cutoff"><div class="hist-head"><span>Model cutoff <strong id="historyDate">{{ ocr.config.snapshot_date }}</strong></span><button type="button" class="quiet" id="historyLatest">Latest</button></div><input type="range" id="historyRange" min="0" max="365" step="1" value="365" aria-label="Release date cutoff"><div class="axis"><span id="rangeStart">2025</span><span id="rangeEnd">{{ ocr.config.snapshot_date }}</span></div><small id="historyStatus">Current model cohort</small></section>
<nav class="views" aria-label="Matrix views"><button type="button" data-view="all" class="active">Matrix</button><button type="button" data-view="structure">Structure</button><button type="button" data-view="robust">Robustness</button><button type="button" data-view="multilingual">Multilingual</button><button type="button" data-view="production">Production</button><button type="button" data-view="secondary">Secondary</button><button type="button" data-view="new">New research</button><button type="button" data-view="recognition">Recognition</button><button type="button" data-view="understanding">Understanding</button><button type="button" data-view="price">Pricing</button></nav>
<section id="matrixPanel"><div class="controls"><input id="modelSearch" type="search" placeholder="Search models…" aria-label="Search models"><select id="coverage" aria-label="Primary evidence coverage">{% for minimum in [1,2,3,4,5] %}<option value="{{ minimum }}"{% if minimum == ocr.config.default_families %} selected{% endif %}>{{ minimum }}+ families</option>{% endfor %}</select><select id="access"><option value="all">All models</option><option value="open">Open weights</option><option value="closed">Closed / hosted</option><option value="unreleased">Unreleased weights</option><option value="unknown">Unknown access</option></select></div>
<div class="table-scroll"><table id="matrixTable"><thead><tr id="matrixHead"><th scope="col">Model</th><th scope="col">Rank index</th>{% for test in ocr.initial.columns %}<th scope="col" title="{{ test.label }}">{{ test.short }}</th>{% endfor %}<th scope="col">$/1k pages</th></tr></thead><tbody id="matrixBody">
{% for row in ocr.initial.rows %}<tr><th scope="row" title="{{ row.name }}">{{ row.name }}</th><td class="index">{{ row | rankCell(ocr.sources) | safe }}</td>{% for test in ocr.initial.columns %}{% set obs = row.scores[test.id] %}{% if obs %}<td class="score" style="--shade:{{ obs.value | shade(ocr.initial.ranges[test.id]) }}" title="{{ obs | scoreTooltip(ocr,row.id,test.id) }}"><a href="{{ ocr.sources[obs.source_id].url }}" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">{{ obs.value | value(test.unit) }}</a>{% if obs.evidence in ['author_reported','vendor_internal','secondary','vendor_comparison','vendor','mixed','imported','research','community'] %}<sup>{% if obs.evidence == 'assumed' %}*{% else %}†{% endif %}</sup>{% endif %}</td>{% else %}<td class="score">—</td>{% endif %}{% endfor %}{% set price = ocr.priceInfoByModel[row.id] %}<td class="price" title="{{ price.note }}">{% if price.source_id %}<a href="{{ ocr.sources[price.source_id].url }}" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">{{ price.label }}</a>{% else %}{{ price.label }}{% endif %}</td></tr>{% endfor %}
</tbody></table></div><p class="key">◊ provisional rank: hover or click for reasons · † qualified evidence / contextual price · — no comparable result. Prices retain their source date in historical views.</p>
</section>
<section id="pricingPanel" hidden>
<h2>Page rates & workload estimates</h2>
<p class="key">Vendor rates, evaluated offerings and benchmark cost estimates are different bases. Compare the provider and mode as well as the number. Current service rates do not guarantee the model generation used in an older benchmark.</p>
<div class="table-scroll"><table class="pricing-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Model / service</th><th scope="col">USD / 1,000 pages</th><th scope="col">Provider & mode</th><th scope="col">Basis / verified</th><th scope="col">Scope & source</th></tr></thead><tbody>
{% for p in ocr.publishedPrices %}<tr><th scope="row">{{ ocr.modelNameById[p.model] }}</th><td>${{ p.usd_per_1000_pages | money }}</td><td>{{ p.provider or 'Not specified' }}<br><small>{{ p.mode }}</small></td><td>{{ p.basis }}<br><small>{{ p.verified_on }}</small></td><td class="pricing-note">{{ p.note or ocr.sources[p.source_id].note }} <a href="{{ ocr.sources[p.source_id].url }}" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Source ↗</a></td></tr>{% endfor %}
</tbody></table></div>
<h2>API token rates</h2>
<p class="key">USD per million tokens. These rates are never converted into an assumed page cost. Input images, page size, reasoning, output length, caching and service tier affect the bill.</p>
<div class="table-scroll"><table class="pricing-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Model</th><th scope="col">Input / 1M</th><th scope="col">Cached input / 1M</th><th scope="col">Output / 1M</th><th scope="col">Provider & mode</th><th scope="col">Scope & source</th></tr></thead><tbody>
{% for p in ocr.tokenPricing %}<tr><th scope="row">{{ ocr.modelNameById[p.model] }}</th><td>${{ p.input_usd_per_million_tokens | money }}</td><td>{% if p.cached_input_usd_per_million_tokens != null %}${{ p.cached_input_usd_per_million_tokens | money }}{% else %}—{% endif %}</td><td>${{ p.output_usd_per_million_tokens | money }}</td><td>{{ p.provider }}<br><small>{{ p.mode }} · {{ p.verified_on }}</small></td><td class="pricing-note">{{ p.note }} <a href="{{ ocr.sources[p.source_id].url }}" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">{{ p.api_model }} ↗</a></td></tr>{% endfor %}
</tbody></table></div>
<details class="method"><summary>Imported prices awaiting source verification</summary><p>These prior observations are preserved as historical context. Their source is the imported snapshot; they are not current verified vendor offers.</p><div class="table-scroll"><table class="pricing-table"><thead><tr><th>Model</th><th>USD / 1,000 pages</th><th>Imported basis</th><th>As of</th><th>Notes</th></tr></thead><tbody>{% for p in ocr.importedPrices %}<tr><th scope="row">{{ ocr.modelNameById[p.model] }}</th><td>${{ p.usd_per_1000_pages | money }}</td><td>{{ p.basis }}</td><td>{{ p.as_of }}</td><td class="pricing-note">{{ p.note }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}</tbody></table></div></details>
<details class="method"><summary>Self-hosted models & unknown page costs</summary><p>Open weights do not mean zero processing cost. Hardware, throughput, electricity, hosting and licenses vary. We do not assign an invented page price.</p><p>{% for m in ocr.selfHostedModels %}{{ m.name }}{% if not loop.last %} · {% endif %}{% endfor %}</p></details>
</section>
<details class="method"><summary>Methodology, provenance & sources</summary><p>Rank is an equal-weight mean of percentiles across mature core families. Maturity requires six scored models from three organizations; one variant per family contributes. Two families permit a provisional index. Three or more remove the limited-coverage qualification; other evidence reasons may still make the rank provisional. The default view requires two primary evidence families.</p><p>Comparable measured public-benchmark results can contribute regardless of operator. Author-reported, vendor/competitor, mixed and unverified evidence qualifies both the affected model and every rank using that comparison cohort. Assumptions and vendor-internal tests never contribute. Correlated variants, small-sample tests, recognition tasks and VQA stay secondary. Published conflicts are preserved and explained. Dates are model release dates; historical views use today's evidence for retrospective cohorts.</p><p>Some older records were migrated from an existing research snapshot; their source links are preserved, but they have not all been independently re-run. Missing model releases are omitted from historic cohorts until the current snapshot.</p><div class="source-grid">{% for id, source in ocr.sources %}<p><a href="{{ source.url }}" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">{{ source.title }}</a> <small>— {{ source.note }}</small></p>{% endfor %}</div></details>
<footer><a href="/">All benchmarks</a> · <a href="https://github.com/voshart/benchmarks">Source repository</a> · Research snapshot {{ ocr.config.snapshot_date }}</footer>
</main><script defer src="/assets/js/ranking.js"></script><script defer src="/assets/js/rank-ui.js"></script><script defer src="/assets/js/bench.js"></script></body></html>
